<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:x="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:excel" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <style>
        body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; }
        table { border-collapse: collapse; }
        th { background-color: #2C3E50; color: #ffffff; font-weight: bold; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid #34495E; text-align: left; font-size: 14px; }
        td { padding: 10px; border: 1px solid #BDC3C7; vertical-align: top; font-size: 12px; color: #333333; }
        .row-even td { background-color: #F8F9F9; }
        .row-odd td { background-color: #FFFFFF; }
        .title-cell { font-weight: bold; color: #2980B9; }
        .client-cell { font-style: italic; color: #7F8C8D; font-weight: bold; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <table>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 120px;">Date</th>
            <th style="width: 150px;">Title</th>
            <th style="width: 200px;">Client</th>
            <th style="width: 300px;">Description</th>
            <th style="width: 250px;">Challenge</th>
            <th style="width: 250px;">Action</th>
            <th style="width: 250px;">Result</th>
        </tr>
        
        <tr class="row-odd">
            <td>2015 - Present</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Financial Advisor</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Public Works Authority 'Ashghal' - Qatar</td>
            <td>Serving as Program Manager and Senior Strategic Advisor, acting as a catalyst for governance enhancement and performance improvement across a major public-sector organization.</td>
            <td>The organization needed to transition to accrual-based accounting (IPSAS) and modernize financial governance.</td>
            <td>Led the strategic alignment between executive business needs and technical ERP capabilities.</td>
            <td>Successfully established a culture of accountability and improved executive visibility into capital deployment.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-even">
            <td>Mar 2015 - Aug 2015</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Management Consultant</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Grant Thornton LLP</td>
            <td>Provided partner-level advisory, focusing on financial governance, organizational transformation, and risk management for diverse clients.</td>
            <td>Client organizations required robust governance and transformation strategies to scale effectively.</td>
            <td>Advised leadership teams on financial controls, process redesign, and enterprise risk management.</td>
            <td>Delivered actionable board-level reporting frameworks and sustainable operational models.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-odd">
            <td>Jun 2014 - Apr 2015</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Business Advisor</td>
            <td class="client-cell">WELCO Group</td>
            <td>Appointed to assess business performance, diagnose organizational inefficiencies, and lead the design of a stronger operating model across a multi-entity group with regional presence.</td>
            <td>Transforming the business from its current state into a more scalable, controlled, and performance-driven future state.</td>
            <td>Conducted enterprise-wide diagnostic review, redesigned organizational structure, and led ERP rollout.</td>
            <td>Improved business planning disciplines and introduced operationally driven financial reporting for management decisions.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-even">
            <td>Aug 2007 - Nov 2013</td>
            <td class="title-cell">VP Finance- Project Financial Controls</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Abu Dhabi Ports Company</td>
            <td>Held VP Finance role leading Project Financial Controls, overseeing financial governance of capital programs exceeding multi-billion-dollar values.</td>
            <td>Managing the financial controls and cash flow forecasting for an unprecedented offshore port mega-project.</td>
            <td>Developed and implemented rigorous project financial controls from scratch.</td>
            <td>Delivered high-fidelity financial visibility to the Board of Directors.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-odd">
            <td>Jul 2006 - Aug 2007</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Financial Planning & Reporting Manager</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Nakheel – UAE</td>
            <td>As Financial Planning & Reporting Manager, delivered comprehensive five-year forecasts for world-class mega projects during a historic expansion phase.</td>
            <td>The rapid scale of development required highly complex, long-term financial modeling.</td>
            <td>Engineered integrated five-year forecasts covering both financial and commercial dimensions.</td>
            <td>Provided the critical data backbone needed for Board-level reporting and investment decisions.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-even">
            <td>Aug 2000 - Jun 2006</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Controller of Accounts</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Major Petroleum & Gas Sector</td>
            <td>Directed financial strategies, budgeting, and performance management for large-scale petroleum operations, ensuring strict compliance and cost control.</td>
            <td>Navigating volatile market conditions while maintaining strict budgetary control over capital-intensive exploration and production projects.</td>
            <td>Implemented comprehensive performance measurement systems and variance analysis frameworks for operational budgeting.</td>
            <td>Optimized cash flow forecasting, eliminated structural inefficiencies, and safeguarded critical investments.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-odd">
            <td>Nov 1992 - Jul 1999</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Senior Accountant</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Ernst & Young</td>
            <td>Provided extensive external audit, financial governance, and advisory services to a wide portfolio of top-tier corporate clients.</td>
            <td>Identify control weaknesses and ensure stringent financial reporting standards for rapidly scaling businesses.</td>
            <td>Led complex audit engagements, assessed risk management protocols, and delivered strategic insights to client management.</td>
            <td>Enhanced corporate financial integrity, minimized operational risks, and established robust internal control foundations.</td>
        </tr>

        <tr class="row-even">
            <td>Nov 1990 - Nov 1992</td>
            <td class="title-cell">Senior Accountant</td>
            <td class="client-cell">Arthur Andersen – Egypt</td>
            <td>Established early career foundation in rigorous financial auditing, internal controls, and enterprise accounting standards at a top global firm.</td>
            <td>Ensuring precise compliance and financial integrity for rapidly scaling corporate clients.</td>
            <td>Executed detailed audits, identified systemic weaknesses in client financial reporting, and recommended robust internal controls.</td>
            <td>Built a strong foundation in forensic accounting, risk mitigation, and executive-level financial reporting.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>
</body>
</html>
